rm-adopted\", \"f-vote-record\"], \"source_ids\": [\"s-raft-candidate-prevote\", \"s-raft-candidate-vote\", \"s-raft-elect-self\"]},\n\nLINE 125 len 1013\n    {\"id\": \"f-vote-record\", \"meaning\": \"The node has durably recorded the vote (T, C) for election term T; a duplicate request for the same (T, C) is re-granted from this record, and a request for a different candidate in T is refused.\", \"identity\": {\"node\": \"local Raft instance\", \"term\": \"T\", \"candidate\": \"C\"}, \"validity_context\": \"Holds for the adopted term T; adopting a greater term makes the record unusable for new grants because the duplicate check only matches the request term.\", \"representation\": [\"StableStore key \\\"LastVoteTerm\\\" through SetUint64\", \"StableStore key \\\"LastVoteCand\\\"\"], \"durability\": \"persisted through StableStore before the vote is granted; a persistence error leaves the vote ungranted\", \"recovery\": \"read back on each RequestVote; not rebuilt from any other state\", \"source_ids\": [\"s-raft-vote-record\", \"s-raft-set-current-term\"], \"unknowns\": [\"whether a stored-term regression could let a second, different candidate be granted in a term in which the node has already voted\"]},\n\n162:    \"rationale\": \"Both core relationships and their connection are explained from actual code: formation and advancement are grounded in the vote tally, the pre-vote round, commitment.match/recalculate and the startIndex own-term rule; context and authority are grounded in the term/state update, leader identity update, the leader lease step-down and TimeoutNow. The connection is sourced: votes are only re-granted for the same term, older-term RPCs are ignored, match indexes are only usable at or after startIndex, and a transfer requires the target to be caught up. Two premises that the first version of this map left as unknowns are now recorded as mechanisms in the behaviors that own them: the transport heartbeat callback performs its term, state and leader writes without being serialized with the main goroutine and publishes the term through a plain atomic store, and a client future for VerifyLeader or a batched Apply carries no shutdown escape once a completed Shutdown has left the buffered request channels unprocessed. The counter-parts that bound each mechanism are recorded beside them (the fast path cannot append logs or advance the commit index; the default unbuffered applyCh always completes, and the leader lease and the replication path cover term discovery), so no core gap is claimed and the overview stays usable.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
